/F1 10.5 Tf 0.20 0.22 0.26 rg 0 -35 Td (The hardest part of getting older that nobody warns you about isn't your own body. It's watching the) Tj
0 -18 Td (chairs around the table empty out one at a time. I've sat with people who stopped making new friends) Tj
0 -18 Td (at sixty because it felt disloyal to the ones they'd lost. Then they had nobody left in the room.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 0.20 0.22 0.26 rg 0 -26 Td (Grief for the people you've lost is real and it deserves its own space, not a bullet point in a workbook.) Tj
0 -18 Td (But staying in the room, making room for new people even while missing the old ones, isn't a betrayal.) Tj
0 -18 Td (It's how you don't end up alone in a chair with nobody sitting in the others.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 0.20 0.22 0.26 rg 0 -26 Td (The table doesn't have to stay set for people who are gone. Set a place for someone new.) Tj
